- assign_compliance_certificate shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha
- confirm_operator_alignment shift_candidate_alpha driver_operator_alpha (requires constraint_applied shift_candidate_alpha)
- verify_compliance_certificate shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha (requires operator_alignment_confirmed and candidate_compliance_certificate_linked)
- release_compliance_certificate shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha (makes certificate available again)
- assign_compliance_certificate shift_candidate_beta compliance_certificate_alpha
- (now we have candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift_candidate_beta compliance_certificate_alpha)
- later establish_clearance_origin_loaded shift_candidate_beta ... (requires candidate_compliance_certificate_linked)

Now we also need to apply operational constraint to shift_candidate_alpha (constraint_applied). We'll do that before alignment.

Now we need to establish clearance for shift_candidate_beta after loading verified.

Now we need to finalize shift_candidate_alpha (candidate_finalized shift_candidate_alpha). There are multiple finalize actions: finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation (requires compliance_validation_complete shift_candidate_alpha, not candidate_finalized), finalize_candidate_direct (requires candidate_clearance_established shift_candidate_alpha, not route_sequence_context_set, not candidate_finalized), finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation (requires candidate_clearance_established, route_sequence_validated, not candidate_finalized). Since we will have compliance_validation_complete shift_candidate_alpha true, we can use finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation. That also sets dispatch_ready shift_candidate_alpha true.

Thus after compliance validation complete, we can finalize shift_candidate_alpha.

Now we need dispatch_allocated, dispatch_ready, dispatched for origin_availability_alpha, destination_availability_alpha, shift_candidate_alpha.

We need to allocate dispatch slots and mark dispatch ready.

We have dispatch_slot_alpha available initially.

We need to allocate dispatch slot to each candidate via allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate (requires dispatch_ready ?candidate, candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile, dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot, not dispatch_allocated ?candidate). So we need each candidate to be dispatch_ready before allocating slot.

Thus we need to make each candidate dispatch_ready via mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready or mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready or maybe there is a generic? There are mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready and mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready. For schedule_candidate (shift_candidate) there is no explicit mark_dispatch_ready; but we have finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation which sets dispatch_ready ?candidate as effect. Also finalize_candidate_direct and finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation set dispatch_ready. So we can make shift_candidate_alpha dispatch_ready via finalize.

For origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha, we have mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready and mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready actions. They require origin_availability_locked, origin_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not dispatch_ready. Similarly for destination.

Thus we need to have transport_leg_assembled and transport_leg_loading_authorized true before marking dispatch ready.

Thus we need to assemble transport leg and authorize loading before we can mark dispatch ready for origin and destination.

Now we also need to execute dispatch (execute_origin_dispatch, execute_destination_dispatch, execute_schedule_dispatch). Those require dispatch_allocated ?candidate, candidate_vehicle_linked ?candidate ?vehicle_unit, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked ?candidate ?dispatch_slot, not dispatched ?candidate. Effects: dispatched ?candidate, vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit, dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot.

Thus we need to allocate dispatch slot before executing dispatch.

Thus order for each candidate:

- Ensure candidate is dispatch_ready (via appropriate action)
- Allocate dispatch slot (allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate)
- Execute dispatch (execute_*_dispatch)

Now we need to ensure we have vehicle linked and allocated for each candidate before dispatch (vehicle_allocated and candidate_vehicle_linked). For origin_availability_alpha we already have vehicle_allocated and vehicle_vehicle_linked to vehicle_unit_alpha (from init). For destination_availability_alpha we need to allocate vehicle_unit_beta and link. For shift_candidate_alpha we already have vehicle_allocated and linked to vehicle_unit_gamma (from init). For shift_candidate_beta we need to allocate vehicle_unit_gamma and link (we will do after freeing from shift_candidate_alpha).

Now we also need to have destination_node_occupied and destination_node_ready true. We'll achieve via activate_destination_node then load_destination_payload.

Now we need to have origin_node_occupied and origin_node_ready true via activate_origin_node then load_origin_payload.

Now we need to have transport_leg_assembled, origin_linked, destination_linked, loading_authorized.

Now we need to have loading_container_loaded loading_container_beta and loading_container_leg_linked loading_container_beta transport_leg_alpha.

Now we need to have candidate_staged_for_loading shift_candidate_beta, candidate_loading_verified shift_candidate_beta.

Now we need to have candidate_clearance_established shift_candidate_beta (via establish_clearance_origin_loaded).

Now we need to have route_sequence_context_set shift_candidate_beta (effect of establish_clearance_origin_loaded). Good.

Now we need to have candidate_finalized shift_candidate_alpha (via finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation).

Now we need to have dispatch_allocated, dispatch_ready, dispatched for each.

Now we need to have vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha (after dispatching origin_availability_alpha). Also vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha (still true after dispatch? Actually after dispatch, vehicle_allocated remains true, vehicle_available becomes true). So we will have both.

Now we need to have vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta (after allocating vehicle_unit_gamma). Also vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_alpha remains true.

Now we need to have vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha (after allocating vehicle_unit_beta).

Now we need to have cargo_available? Goal does not require cargo_available; after loading payloads, cargo_available becomes false (since payloads are linked). That's fine.

Now we need to have loading_container_loaded loading_container_beta true (we will have after loading container onto leg). Goal requires loading_container_loaded loading_container_beta true. Good.

Now we need to have loading_container_leg_linked loading_container_beta transport_leg_alpha true (after loading container onto leg). Good.

Now we need to have transport_leg_assembled transport_leg_alpha true (after assembling leg). Also transport_leg_origin_linked and destination_linked true.

Now we need to have transport_leg_loading_authorized true (after authorize).

Now we need to have origin_node_occupied and origin_node_ready true (after activation and loading). Destination similarly.

Now we need to have origin_availability_confirmed and locked true (after load_origin_payload sets origin_availability_confirmed true and origin_availability_locked true). Good.

Now we need to have destination_availability_confirmed and locked true (after load_destination_payload sets those true). Good.

Now we need to have dispatch_allocated for each candidate after allocating slot.

Now we need to have dispatch_ready for each before allocating slot.

Now we need to have dispatched after executing dispatch.

Now we need to have candidate_finalized shift_candidate_alpha true.

Now we need to have candidate_clearance_established shift_candidate_beta true.

Now we need to have compliance_validation_complete shift_candidate_alpha true.

Now we need to have constraint_applied shift_candidate_alpha true.

Now we need to have operator_alignment_confirmed shift_candidate_alpha true.

Now we need to have candidate_loading_verified shift_candidate_beta true.

Now we need to have candidate_staged_for_loading shift_candidate_beta true.

Now we need to have candidate_skill_certificate_linked shift_candidate_beta skill_certificate_alpha true.

Now we need to have candidate_task_profile_linked shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha true.

Now we need to have candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta true.

Now we need to have candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha true.

Now we need to have candidate_prepared destination_availability_alpha true.

Now we need to have candidate_dispatch_slot_linked for each candidate to dispatch_slot_alpha.

Now we need to have candidate_vehicle_linked destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta true.

Now we need to have candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_beta vehicle_unit_gamma true.

Now we need to have vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha true.

Now we need to have vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta true.

Now we need to have vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha true (after dispatching origin).

Now we need to have vehicle_allocated origin_availability_alpha true (still true after dispatch? Actually after dispatch, vehicle_allocated remains true; we never deallocate). So fine.

Now we need to have vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_alpha true (still true). Good.

Now we need to have vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha true (we will allocate).

Now we need to have vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta true (we will allocate).

Now we need to have vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha true (after dispatch origin). Also vehicle_available vehicle_unit_beta? Not required but will be true after dispatch destination; vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma? Not required but will be true after dispatch shift_candidate_alpha? Actually we will dispatch shift_candidate_alpha as well, making vehicle_unit_gamma available. Goal does not require vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma, but that's okay.

Now we need to have dispatch_slot_available dispatch_slot_alpha after all dispatches? Actually each dispatch makes dispatch_slot_available true again (effect). So after three dispatches, it will be available again. Goal does not require dispatch_slot_available; it's not in goal. So fine.

Now we need to ensure we don't violate any negative preconditions.

